      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that it can look like a rational choice when framed purely as efficiency—zero versus zero. But rationality isn't only about minimizing pain; it's also about maximizing *potential* experiences, even if they're temporary. The cycle isn't truly meaningless if it contains moments of genuine connection, beauty, or growth that you haven't yet encountered. And while opting out ends the pain, it also permanently closes the door on any future variable that might tip the scale. You don't have to believe in a grand meaning to give yourself permission to stay curious about what comes next.",
